: null, "accordionData": null, "includeSeconds": null, "selectedModalId": 0, "textCarouselData": "{ \"text\": [] }", "checkListTextData": null, "imageCarouselData": null, "checklistImageData": null, "clickableAlphabetData": null}, {"id": 44050073, "text": "<h2>Tips:</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Remember, ‘who’, ‘whose’ and ‘whom’ must refer to a person or named animal.</li>\n<li>If you get stuck, think about your basic sentence first, e.g. ‘The ball was lying on the sand.’ Then add in a relative pronoun that fits and think of your <span style=\"color:#F28D00\">relative clause</span>, e.g. ‘The ball that <span style=\"color:#F28D00\">____________</span> was lying on the sand.’</li>\n<li>Think about whether you need commas around your relative clause:\n<ul>\n<li>You <b>don’t</b> need commas if your <span style=\"color:#F28D00\">relative clause</span> is essential to help us know which person/thing/place you are talking about, e.g.: \n<br><i>He saw the seagull <span style=\"color:#F28D00\">that was nearest the lighthouse</span>.</i> </li>\n<li>You <b>do</b> need commas if the <span style=\"color:#F28D00\">relative clause</span> is just adding extra information, e.g.: \n<br><i>The sky, <span style=\"color:#F28D00\">which was as blue as the sea</span>, stretched out towards the horizon.</i></li>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</ul>\n", "modal": {"steps": [null], "details": null}, "order": 5, "btnType": null, "linkUrl": null, "audioUrl": null, "fileName": null, "fontSize": null, "fontType": "SassoonInfantRg-Regular", "imageUrl": null, "linkName": null, "stepType": "TEXT_AND_IMAGE", "tabsData": null, "deletedAt": null, "tableData": "{'headers':['Col1'],'rows':[{'col1':'row1'},{'col1':'row2'}, {'col1':'row3'}]}", "timerData": null, "activityId": 44049502, "dimensions": null, "editAsHtml": false, "properties": {"height": "", "fontArray": [[]], "inputArray": [[]], "widthArray": [[""]]}, "deletedById": null, "downloadUrl": null, "editorState": null, "carouselData": null, "downloadName": null, "accordionDa